title: Abolishment of Subsidies and Price Controls.
subtitle: The <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap drop-down">Nitti government<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/FrancescoSaverioNitti.png">In Government: PSRI, [+ ldr_name +], [+ ul_name +], PPI, [+ ds_name +]</span></span> floors a controversial bill.
tags: event, govt_affairs
is-card: true
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 6 and week = 1 and prime_minister = "Nitti"
on-arrival: {!
Q.yes_votes = 0;
Q.no_votes = 0;
Q.abstain_votes = 0;
Q.ul_opinion = "Si";
Q.bread_price_seen = 1;
Q.psri_opinion = "No";
Q.pri_opinion = "No";
Q.ds_opinion = "Si";
Q.ppi_opinion = "No";
Q.ldr_opinion = "Si";
Q.pnf_opinion = "No";
Q.other_opinion = "Abstain";
!}
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
face-image: img/bread.jpeg

= Abolishment Of Subsidies and Price Controls

The <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap drop-down">Nitti government<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/FrancescoSaverioNitti.png">In Government: PSRI, [+ ldr_name +], [+ ul_name +], PPI, [+ ds_name +]</span></span> has floored a bill that would abolish price controls on essential goods, including a controversial abolishing of price controls on bread, due to the crippling deficit that <span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**a**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**ly**</span> is starting to gain. However, this bill is not popular among the left wing parties, specifically the PSI, PSRI, PRI, some members of the PPI and dissident socialists spread across the Others, and our support base, the workers, and many in our party leadership are calling for us to vote agaisnt the bill.

Already, a general strike has been called by several unions under the PSI.

What should we do?

- @vote_yes: Vote yes, abolishing the price controls on bread.
- @vote_no: Vote no, against abolishing the price controls on bread.
- @abstain: Abstain from the vote.

@vote_yes
on-arrival: communist_dissent += 10; labour_dissent += 5; maximalist_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5; syndicalist_dissent += 5; workers_pcdi += 6 if pcdi_formed; workers_psi -= 7; vote_yes_bread_fixing = 1

Our party members are shocked by our betrayal of the workers in order to side with a clearly unpopular policy! Some even begin dissenting and many Communist and Labour members have defected to the No! side. Party leadership is also infuriated, with even some Reformist members of our party calling this a bad idea.

- @vote_bread: The Chamber Of Deputies votes on the proposal..

@vote_no
on-arrival: ul_relation -= 10; ldr_relation -= 5; communist_dissent -= 5; labour_dissent -= 5; workers_psi += 3*(1-dissent); vote_no_bread_fixing = 1

Most of our party leadership are relieved, along with the workers which support us, and they appreciate the vote agaisnt the bill, however  some of our contacts with the [+ ul_name +] and the [+ ldr_name +] have stopped talking to us, most likely due to our decision.

- @bread_menu_no: Negotiations start between us and the other parties about the bill.

@abstain
on-arrival: ul_relation -= 5; ldr_relation -= 3; communist_dissent += 5; labour_dissent += 5; workers_psi -= 3*(1-dissent); abstain_bread_fixing = 1

Our party members AND the [+ ul_name +] and [+ ldr_name +] are shocked at our decisionmaking! What were we thinking? Are we hoping the Abstain side will somehow win? Well, it doesnt matter now..

- @vote_bread: The Chamber Of Deputies votes on the proposal..

@bread_menu_no

- @convince_ds_wow: Attempt to convince the [+ ds_name +] to vote agaisnt the bill.
- @convince_ldr_wow: Attempt to convince the [+ ldr_name +] to vote agaisnt the bill.
- @convince_other_wow: Attempt to convince the Others.
- @vote_bread: We have done enough.

@convince_ldr_wow
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ldr_relation < 65) {
    Q.ldr_opinion = "Si";
}
if (Q.ldr_relation > 75) {
    Q.ldr_opinion = "No";
}
!}
go-to: bread_menu_no
max-visits: 1

[? if ldr_opinion = "Si": Unfortunately, and perhaps unsurprisingly, the LDR and its leader have voted in favour of the law, though some claim that voting for it would be pointless since the war already seems doomed.  ?]

[? if ldr_opinion = "No": Thankfully, the LDR has realized the unpopularity of the bill and has voted agaisnt after having previously favoured the Si option, being swayed by its left wing. ?]

@convince_ds_wow
subtitle: [? if ds_leader = "Carnazza" or ds_leader = "Colonna" : We shouldn't be optimistic about their response. ?]
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ds_leader == "Giuffrida") {
        Q.ds_opinion = "No"
}
!}
go-to: bread_menu_no
max-visits: 1

[? if ds_opinion = "No": Thankfully, the [+ ds_name +] has told us they are to vote agaisnt the bill! ?] [? if ds_opinion = "Si": Unfortunately, the [+ ds_name +] will be voting for the bill. ?]

@convince_other_wow
view-if: not pri_prominent or psri_collapse
on-arrival: other_opinion = "No"
go-to: bread_menu_no
max-visits: 1

We contact the left-leaning minor parties, specifically the [? if not pri_prominent : PRI ?] [? if pri_prominent and psri_collapse : and the ?] [? if psri_collapse : PSRI ?], who agree to vote against the bill.


@vote_bread
on-arrival: {!

if (Q.vote_yes_bread_fixing == 1) {
    Q.yes_votes += Q.psi_seating -= Q.communist_strength & Q.labour_strength;
}
if (Q.vote_yes_bread_fixing == 1) {
    Q.no_votes += Q.communist_strength & Q.labour_strength;
}
if (Q.vote_no_bread_fixing == 1) {
    Q.no_votes += Q.psi_seating;
}
if (Q.abstain_bread_fixing == 1) {
    Q.abstain_votes += Q.psi_seating -= Q.communist_strength & Q.labour_strength;
}
if (Q.abstain_bread_fixing == 1) {
    Q.no_votes += Q.communist_strength & Q.labour_strength;
}
if (Q.pll_formed == 1) {
    Q.no_votes += Q.pll_seating;
}
if (Q.pcs_formed == 1) {
    Q.yes_votes += Q.pcs_seating;
}
if (Q.cc_formed == 1) {
    Q.yes_votes += Q.cc_seating;
}
if (Q.pcdi_formed == 1) {
    Q.no_votes += Q.pcdi_seating;
}
if (Q.psu_formed == 1) {
    Q.no_votes += Q.psu_seating;
}
if (Q.psri_opinion == "Abstain") {
    Q.abstain_votes += Q.psri_seating;
}
if (Q.psri_opinion == "Si") {
    Q.yes_votes += Q.psri_seating;
}
if (Q.psri_opinion == "No") {
    Q.no_votes += Q.psri_seating;
}
if (Q.pri_opinion == "Abstain") {
    Q.abstain_votes += Q.pri_seating;
}
if (Q.pri_opinion == "Si") {
    Q.yes_votes += Q.pri_seating;
}
if (Q.pri_opinion == "No") {
    Q.no_votes += Q.pri_seating;
}
if (Q.ds_opinion == "Abstain") {
    Q.abstain_votes += Q.ds_seating;
}
if (Q.ds_opinion == "Si") {
    Q.yes_votes += Q.ds_seating;
}
if (Q.ds_opinion == "No") {
    Q.no_votes += Q.ds_seating;
}
if (Q.ppi_opinion == "Abstain") {
    Q.abstain_votes += Q.ppi_seating;
}
if (Q.ppi_opinion == "Si") {
    Q.yes_votes += Q.ppi_seating;
}
if (Q.ppi_opinion == "No") {
    Q.no_votes += Q.ppi_seating;
}
if (Q.ldr_opinion == "Abstain") {
    Q.abstain_votes += Q.ldr_seating;
}
if (Q.ldr_opinion == "Si") {
    Q.yes_votes += Q.ldr_seating;
}
if (Q.ldr_opinion == "No") {
    Q.no_votes += Q.ldr_seating;
}
if (Q.ul_opinion == "Si") {
    Q.yes_votes += Q.ul_seating;
}
if (Q.pnf_opinion == "Abstain") {
    Q.abstain_votes += Q.pnf_seating;
}
if (Q.pnf_opinion == "Si") {
    Q.yes_votes += Q.pnf_seating;
}
if (Q.pnf_opinion == "No") {
    Q.no_votes += Q.pnf_seating;
}
if (Q.other_opinion == "Abstain") {
    Q.abstain_votes += Q.other_seating;
}
if (Q.other_opinion == "Si") {
    Q.yes_votes += Q.other_seating;
}
if (Q.other_opinion == "No") {
    Q.no_votes += Q.other_seating;
}

Q.yes_percent = parseFloat((Q.yes_votes / 2).toFixed(1));
Q.no_percent = parseFloat((Q.no_votes / 2).toFixed(1));
Q.abstain_percent = parseFloat((Q.abstain_votes / 2).toFixed(1));
!}
on-display: {!
data = []
if (Q.no_votes) {
    data.push({
        "id": "nó",
        "legend": "No",
        "name": "No",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.no_votes),
    });
}
if (Q.yes_votes) {
    data.push({
        "id": "si",
        "legend": "Si",
        "name": "Si",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.yes_votes),
    });
}
if (Q.abstain_votes) {
    data.push({
        "id": "astenersi",
        "legend": "Astenersi",
        "name": "Astenersi",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.abstain_votes),
    });
}
             
if (window && d3) {
    var width = 500; 
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50; 
        height = width;
        document.getElementById("chamber").style.height = screenWidth/2 + "px";
    } 

    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select("#chamber").datum(data).call(parliament);
}
!}

= Voting

{!<svg id="chamber" style="width: 500px; height: 250px;"> </svg>!}

Si - [+ yes_votes +] votes 

<span style="color: #FF746C;">**No**</span> - [+ no_votes +] votes 

Astenersi - [+ abstain_votes +] votes 

- @yay: The bill is shot down.
- @huhabstain: The bill is shot down via abstain votes.
- @how_could_you_do_this: The bill passes and is signed into law.

@yay
subtitle: Predictable.
view-if: no_votes >= yes_votes and abstain_votes

The bill, as expected, has been shot down, and the bill will not become law. What a close call. The governing coalition is seeming unstable.

@how_could_you_do_this
subtitle: The workers are furious. 
view-if: yes_votes >= no_votes and abstain_votes if abstain_votes > 0

Somehow, the bill has passed the Chamber Of Deputies. Members of our party are mad, that we didnt do more to stop the bill, that we even collaborate with parties that do this. However, the governing coalition has mostly suffered from this as dissent inmediately brews among the PPI, PSRI, LDR, UL, etc.

- @root: Good riddance.

@huhabstain
subtitle: An unexpected result?
view-if: abstain_votes >= yes_votes and no_votes
on-arrival: radicalism += 1

Somehow, the abstain option has won, hurting the governments legitimacy and raising radicalism. The governing coalition is seeming unstable.
